<%/* What the plan does by itself, and what it leaves to the person. It
     starts each of this person's steps once what it waits for is merged
     (another's start on their computer), and sends a design
     or discussion session its first message (R-s6t). Merging waits for the
     person unless they let the plan do it, which only a project with no
     remote can: with a remote, each step is pushed for a pull request, and
     a push always asks (R-p4h). The card is a region; ticking saves it and
     answers with the card. */%>
<% const p = it, base = `/f/${p.project.id}/plans/${p.id}`, alone = p.mergeAlone === true || p.mergeAlone === 'true'; %>
<h2 id="settings-title">By itself</h2>
<ul class="stack gap-2">
  <li class="secondary">Starts each of your steps on this computer once the steps it waits for are merged into main, bringing its branch up to date first. Other people’s start on theirs.</li>
  <li class="secondary">Sends a design or discussion its first message. The rest of that session is its owner’s.</li>
  <li class="secondary">Leaves a step nobody owns for someone to claim.</li>
</ul>
<% if (p.remote) { %>
<p class="secondary">Never pushes. When a step is ready to finish, you push it to <code><%= p.remote.name %></code> for a pull request, and the plan carries on once it’s merged on <%= p.remote.host %>.</p>
<% } else if (p.status !== 'done') { %>
<form class="stack gap-2" action="<%= base %>/settings" method="post" ko-target="planSettings" ko-invoke="change">
  <input type="hidden" name="mergeAlone" value="false">
  <label class="choice"><input type="checkbox" name="mergeAlone" value="true"<% if (alone) { %> checked<% } %>> <span>Merge each step into main when it’s done <span class="muted">· screens approved, or every story built with the check passing. Otherwise it asks you.</span></span></label>
  <noscript><button class="btn small" type="submit">Save</button></noscript>
</form>
<% } else { %>
<p class="secondary"><%= alone ? 'Merged each step into main when it was done.' : 'Asked you before merging each step.' %></p>
<% } %>
